{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-2129",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have a product of a positive number $(5)$ and a negative number $(-5).$ So the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n5\\cdot (-5)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $5$ by $5$ without any signs: $5\\cdot 5=25.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n5\\cdot (-5)=-25.\n$$",
